# The last migration that was applied BY HAND, before scripts/migrate.sh took
# over. On a database with no schema_migrations table, the runner records every
# file up to and including this one as already applied, and RUNS everything
# after it.
#
# Why this file has to exist
# --------------------------
# Baselining the whole directory would mark a migration that has never run as
# "applied" and skip it forever — which on the first automated deploy would
# mean 36_proposal_reports.sql was recorded without being executed, and the new
# code 500ing on a table that does not exist.
#
# It is read ONCE, on the first run against a given database. After that the
# schema_migrations table is authoritative and this file is inert, so it does
# not need updating when you add migrations — only if you ever point the runner
# at another hand-built database.
#
# Blank or missing means "baseline nothing": every migration runs. That is the
# right default for a fresh database and the safe default for an unknown one.
35_proposal_agreements_and_unread.sql
